    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0053" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/5–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consual at Hanoi</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">O’Sullivan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-14">May 14, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received May 15—3:25
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Viet Nam Delegation to Dalat arrived in Hanoi May 12 by plane. Next step will
                    be to send Viet Nam Delegation to Paris to <pb facs="0054" n="42" xml:id="pg42"
                    /> undertake formal negotiations there. Viet Nam Delegation which at present is
                    in France is only good will mission and has no political powers. Impression
                    given following return of Viet Nam Delegation from Dalat is that Dalat
                    Conference gave both parties opportunity to explain their positions and for this
                    reason had a certain value. However, comparatively little progress was made to
                    reconcile divergent views on political, economic or cultural questions.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Sullivan</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
